WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.179 --> 00:00:04.009
Joaquin Phoenix is finally letting us all
in on the joke.

00:00:04.009 --> 00:00:08.800
Once just an outlandish idea, Phoenix's grounded,
lower-budget origin movie for the DC Comics

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:12.680
villain The Joker has gotten an official greenlight
from Warner Brothers.

00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:16.250
With the movie revving toward production,
the actor finally broke his silence in an

00:00:16.250 --> 00:00:20.190
interview with Collider about his motivations
for taking on the role.

00:00:20.190 --> 00:00:23.830
Phoenix revealed that years ago, he had a
similar idea to make a small character-study

00:00:23.830 --> 00:00:26.380
film centered around a comic book villain.

00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:30.250
He was hesitant to tackle the Joker, since
it's been done so many times already, and

00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:31.890
he ended up letting the idea go.

00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:35.000
But things changed once he heard this particular
take on it.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:36.000
He explained,

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:40.050
"I was like, 'Oh that's so exciting, that's
the kind of experience I wanted to have, with

00:00:40.050 --> 00:00:41.850
a movie based on a comic character.'

00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:43.809
I felt like you could get something on screen."

00:00:43.809 --> 00:00:48.170
Phoenix's Joker is being developed in tandem
with another solo Joker movie starring Jared

00:00:48.170 --> 00:00:49.170
Leto.

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:52.920
Leto's will be set inside established DC Extended
Universe continuity, while Phoenix's will

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:57.370
be a standalone film that he says will be
more genre-blurring than the typical "superhero

00:00:57.370 --> 00:00:58.370
movie."

00:00:58.370 --> 00:01:02.600
Phoenix's film is expected to be released
under a new DC Films banner, which, according

00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:06.840
to The Hollywood Reporter, will be called
something along the lines of "DC Dark" or

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:07.840
"DC Black".

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:11.680
Should his version do well with audiences,
it could spark a shift in how studios tell

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:15.530
comic book stories, and help make a more low-key
approach viable.

00:01:15.530 --> 00:01:16.530
Phoenix told Collider,

00:01:16.530 --> 00:01:20.090
"I think, underneath the excitement of these
films, and the size of them, there are these

00:01:20.090 --> 00:01:22.970
incredible characters that are dealing with
real life struggles.

00:01:22.970 --> 00:01:25.670
[...] [They] deserve the opportunity to be
kind of studied."

00:01:25.670 --> 00:01:29.890
Phoenix's Joker film, directed by Todd Phillips
and written by Phillips and Scott Silver,

00:01:29.890 --> 00:01:32.710
is anticipated to be in theaters as soon as
2019.

